seg-d5640ad2cd08 = <c1/> (the default) takes Table { "1" } inside { "1800" } AD to { "2050" } AD and Tables 2a/2b outside it; <c2/> and <c3/> force one. Pluto outside its table is an error, not an extrapolation. The epoch is an ISO { "8601" } date and time in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC), converted through Terrestrial Time (TT) with the leap seconds to Barycentric Dynamical Time (TDB), or a TDB Julian date given directly with <c4/>.

